# NOTICE

## What this project owes to others

LyriMusic is an independent implementation. No source code was copied into it
from any other lyrics client, and no lyrics are distributed by it.

The design was informed by studying how other clients solve the same problem —
in particular [BitChord](https://github.com/kushagrasinghx/BitChord) (GPL-3.0),
whose provider set and lookup strategy were read as prior art. BitChord is
licensed under the GPL-3.0; **no BitChord code, in any form, is included here**.
The architecture is deliberately different (a browser extension in TypeScript
against a structured `LyricsProvider` interface, rather than an Android client),
and the parsers, the lookup, and the clock are original. This project is MIT
licensed and must stay free of GPL-derived code.

The in-page panel exists in the same problem space as
[Better Lyrics](https://github.com/better-lyrics/better-lyrics) and as the
"Lyrics for YouTube Music" extension by *msj*. Their *behaviour* was observed
from the outside; their code was not read for this work and none of it is used.

## Third-party services

Queries are sent, from the user's own browser and on the user's own connection,
to third-party lyrics databases. This project has no relationship with any of
them, hosts none of their content, and proxies none of their traffic:

- [LRCLIB](https://lrclib.net) — open, documented API
- [lyrics.ovh](https://lyrics.ovh) — open API
- [KuGou](https://www.kugou.com) — unofficial
- [NetEase Cloud Music](https://music.163.com) — unofficial

The KuGou and NetEase routes are unofficial and are **disabled by default**. A
user who enables them does so on their own behalf, under those services' terms.

